lesson='''## Deepwell glazing, vapor and pipeline candidate — 2026-10-25

The user reports that v2 window masking needs to be much better, then requests foreground coffee/pipe steam, distant-container steam and perhaps pipeline running lights. V3 is a correction/addition candidate, not accepted motion. The old rectangles both missed full glass and covered parts of pillars/stone. Trace actual panes at fractional source coordinates, supersample coverage and feather inward rather than Gaussian-blurring across frames. Preserve mullions, broad structural pillars, sills and a steady unlit pane. Include white lamp cores as well as warm glazing. In one tiny opening, x1573/y204 was a bright core rather than the proposed stile; actual dark stile is x1570. Explicit source-pixel/core controls and source/mask/all-dim close-ups corrected that mistake before delivery. Current v3 maps ten animated panes in six light groups plus one steady pane. Numeric guards supplement the image review; they do not certify every hand-traced edge artistically.

Coffee provides a plausible foreground vapor source without inventing a pipe leak. Attach the plume inside the cup opening, preserve its front rim/body, and use separate roof-outlet interpretations for process steam on distant tanks. Rising density features and birth-time emission variation avoid fading a stationary smoke stripe. Clip vapor behind vessel/pipe solids, keep outside drift consistent, and use finite height tapers and lifetimes dividing the loop. The first strength setting was too faint in assistant full-composition still review; its study and selected settings are retained. Fixed small pipe-face indicators can carry a travelling acknowledgement pattern without a glowing band drifting through space. Follow the actual visible tube and stop at the plant inlet, rather than copying an old broad protection path onto the cliff. User authorization for indicators supersedes source-pixel invariance only inside their defined core/halo/housing mask; other supports and vessel/cup solids remain protected.

Earlier lessons remain: v1 warm reflections froze under an overbroad water colour gate, rounded screen updates caused a seam spike, and broad water waves softened detail. V2's first soft weather was too faint; coherent terrain-guided moving wisps replaced it. A surface-drift mask later touched 34 support pixels because only airborne haze shared the pipe blocker; fix all relevant masks and retain named source guards. "300% better" expressed ambition, not a measured improvement. Current v3 retains twelve other v2 layers and scoped composites with exact sampled controls, complete frame/timestamp/quiet-neighbour/repeat/direct-YUV checks and exact v2 file preservation. Assistant inspected source/masks/temporal/decoded stills, not continuous playback. User artistic verdict remains pending. [V3 evidence](../music/deepwell-animation-v3/README.md), [v2 history](../music/deepwell-animation-v2/README.md), [v1 history](../music/deepwell-animation-v1/README.md).
'''
